{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation of `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`.\n\n- **Separate record per assessment under `<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json`:**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` checks the file name equals `run_id`. It also checks that a second run adds a second file and leaves the first byte-identical.\n  - `confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record`, the batch test with 6 and then 7 records, and `citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations` (distinct run ids) cover one record per assessment.\n- **State location, cited as `requirements.configuration.state_location`:**\n  - The same test uses `XDG_STATE_HOME` and expects the record under `habeas/authoring/usage`.\n  - It also checks that an uncreatable or undeterminable state location fails with a stderr diagnostic. It checks stdout stays empty and the existing evidence is preserved.\n- **Required fields:**\n  - The same test asserts `version`, `run_id`, `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, `start_time_ms <= end_time_ms`, and `evidence_output`.\n  - `usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared` and `usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind` cover subject kinds and null backend/model before they are known.\n- **Determination kind:**\n  - `false_is_a_completed_assessment` asserts `false`.\n  - `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` asserts `FIXME`.\n  - `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` asserts `true`, `false` and `FIXME`.\n  - Failed runs have a null determination (`missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence`).\n- **`evidence_output` and `evidence_written`:**\n  - `file` and `true` are asserted in the ollama and batch tests.\n  - `stdout` and `true` are asserted in `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files`.\n  - `stdout` with `false` on failure is asserted in `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence`.\n  - `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage` asserts `evidence_written` is false after a failed write.\n- **Usage outside the project in stdout mode:** `usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it` covers both default and `--stdout` modes. It checks for a refusal, that the directory is not created, and that the existing evidence is unchanged.\n- **No FIXME entry text:** the ollama test asserts the serialized usage does not contain `#125`.\n- **Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs stay distinguishable:**\n  - `unfinished_runs_are_visible_before_the_backend_is_selected` asserts `unfinished` with a null `end_time_ms` and `evidence_written` false.\n  - `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause` asserts `failed` and `cancelled` with an end time and no determination.\n  - `interrupted_terminal_progress_keeps_unstarted_work_incomplete` (via `assert_interruption_stops_the_batch`) asserts `cancelled` records with `evidence_written` false.\n  - The batch failure tests assert `failed` records.\n- **No source text, prompts, responses or rationale:** the ollama test asserts the serialized usage lacks the secret requirement, definition, source and rationale strings and the credential.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no untested obligations.",
  "references": "8c266bd14ae66b5b7651841b71fae50faddc6c6ad08ec107580bad7462d9a96b",
